From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 06:19:20 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fixup! validation: prepare decoded RPC transaction checks
 before cs_main

Recover persistent batch decoder workers and reuse transaction-ID strings from the selected original 5a626227c2754aac5ac90f368a3c0ac572744bad RPC hunks. Historical shared036 omitted the persistent scheduling body; final native128 already supplies its own signing-worker implementation.

Use the host-neutral bounded ParallelRangeExecutor prerequisite rather than requiring the later staged-admission API or native signing. Keep context-free PrecomputeSingleTxData at its existing owner70 boundary, array index order, first malformed input, and caller-thread fallback under contention. Cache each decoded ID once for result rows and single-item effective-includes.

Prepared regression coverage exercises alternating malformed and decodable batches through both RPCs, checking first-error text, ID order and no partial admission. Compilation and tests have not run; coordinator grant pending.
